Provenance and third-party attributions.

1. fullwave lineage
   The Python pipeline (io_dat, geom, medium, sim) and the raw .dat I/O
   contract derive from G. Pinton's fullwave solver lineage. The optimized CUDA
   solver EXECUTABLES are NOT part of this package -- they are built and distributed
   separately and fetched at runtime (see fullwave2_ultra.solver.resolve_binary).
   This Python pipeline is licensed under Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). The separately
   distributed solver executables are NOT covered by Apache-2.0; they are licensed
   under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 (see LICENSE-binaries.txt) -- free for
   academic/noncommercial use, commercial use requires a separate license.

2. MACH beamformer (optional dependency, not vendored)
   FSA beamforming uses MACH (mach-beamform), (c) 2025 Forest Neurotech, The Clear BSD
   License, github.com/Forest-Neurotech/mach. Installed via pip (the [beamform] extra);
   not redistributed here. Required only at call time by beamform.beamform_fsa.

3. Datasets (NOT redistributed)
   The LLZ abdominal FSA dataset, the microCT CarteGianmarco20um volume, and any
   Verasonics data are third-party, read-only, of unknown redistribution rights. They
   are NOT committed; examples regenerate synthetic fixtures on demand. Only the tiny
   synthetic 2D fixture inputs under examples/tiny_nsims4/ are tracked (golden parity
   reference); no measured data is included.

4. CUDA device/driver introspection (fullwave2_ultra/cuda_utils.py)
   The ctypes-based libcuda introspection (device specs, compute capability, driver
   version) is adapted from fullwave25 (github.com/pinton-lab/fullwave25,
   fullwave/solver/cuda_utils.py), itself derived from a public gist by f0k
   (gist.github.com/f0k/63a664160d016a491b2cbea15913d549, the
   permalink_comment_id=5043495 update). The solver preflight + binary-resolution
   (fullwave2_ultra/solver.py) follow the same project's binary_manager/ensure_binary
   pattern.
